abstract: >-
  One Bash file that sends Telegram messages from terminals, coding agents and research scripts,
  with curl as its only hard requirement: milestones, code and tables, formulas typeset on the
  machine, figures and pages of PDF files, and reports on long computations, which it can watch
  for stalls and warning words. It can also ask a question and return the answer typed or tapped
  on the phone, receive a file sent from the phone, and say on every message which machine, which
  agent and which project is speaking. Configuration files are parsed and never executed, and the
  token of the bot is never printed nor taken from the folder in which it runs.
